title: 'pallet-revive: validate eth_feeHistory reward percentiles'

doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    `eth_feeHistory` did not validate the requested reward percentiles: out-of-range values
    were silently clamped to `0..=100` and unsorted lists were accepted, so a malformed request
    returned approximated results instead of an error. As in go-ethereum, each reward percentile
    must now lie within `0.0..=100.0` and the list must be strictly increasing; otherwise the
    request is rejected.

crates:
- name: pallet-revive-eth-rpc
  bump: patch
